          <h3>WebArena Verified · shopping admin</h3>
          <p>{verifiedNavigationCount} navigation episodes on synthetic Magento admin data produced {verifiedNavigationSuccesses} full task successes, {verifiedNavigationPartial} partial rewards, and {verifiedNavigationCount - verifiedNavigationSuccesses - verifiedNavigationPartial} zero rewards. No task timed out. Mean reward is {verifiedNavigationRun.meanReward.toFixed(3)}; the initial same-task baseline was {verifiedNavigationBaselineMeanReward.toFixed(3)}. Two theme settings tasks reached full reward with row-specific link context. When a decision sees a changing page fingerprint, the browser now waits up to 1.05 seconds for DOM readiness and network idle before retrying with a fresh snapshot. A focused working-tree follow-up now routes tasks 711 and 713 to Product Views and Bestsellers, fills both explicit date ranges, and clicks Show Report. Both filtered routes still earn only 0.5 reward; the reason for the remaining partial score is unresolved. See the route-only and date-filter traces below. This single-site subset is not a full WebArena score.</p>
          <code>BrowserGym 0.14.3 · Windows CPU + SSH B Docker · full {verifiedNavigationSuccesses}/{verifiedNavigationCount} · partial {verifiedNavigationPartial} · end-to-end p50/p95 {(verifiedNavigationRun.latencyMs.p50 / 1000).toFixed(3)}/{(verifiedNavigationRun.latencyMs.p95 / 1000).toFixed(3)} s · decision-call p95 {verifiedNavigationDecisionP95} ms (n={verifiedNavigationRun.decisionCallLatencyMs.sampleCount})</code>
          <p>A separate working-tree run of BrowserGym Verified task 157 reached full reward 1.0 in two actions. Decision/action calls took 317 ms and 818 ms; the 14.066-second total includes an 11.236-second environment reset. This single read-only task does not change the 18-task aggregate or establish general speed. See the <a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/results/webarena-verified-docker-b-157-post-inspection-followup-20261002.json">raw task 157 trace ↗</a>. A separate BrowserGym Lite task 157 smoke against the Verified backend returned 0.0 because the route stayed on the dashboard; this cross-backend result is not a canonical Lite score. See its <a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/results/webarena-lite-compat-shopping-admin-inspection-pending-20261002.json">raw trace ↗</a>.</p>
          <p>A separate synthetic 57-link choice repeated ten times took 317 ms on the first local CPU call and p50/p95 135/146 ms across nine warm calls. It measures the provider only, repeats one question, and does not include page inspection or actions; its low confidence was uncalibrated. See the <a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/fixtures/browser-choice-latency-57.jsonl">fixture</a> and <a href="https://github.com/krmdl/agent-decision-kit/blob/main/benchmarks/results/browser-choice-latency-57-cpu-20261002.json">raw report</a>.</p>
          <p>A previous run of these same task IDs reported end-to-end p50/p95 {(verifiedNavigationPreviousRun.latencyMs.p50 / 1000).toFixed(3)}/{(verifiedNavigationPreviousRun.latencyMs.p95 / 1000).toFixed(3)} s and decision-call p95 {verifiedNavigationPreviousDecisionP95} ms (n={verifiedNavigationPreviousRun.decisionCallLatencyMs.sampleCount}). This pair of runs does not establish a general speed gain.</p>
